<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jeroboam I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jeroboam I was the first king of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-israel">Kingdom of Israel</a>, reigning from about 931 to 910 BCE according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>. A former overseer of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a>'s forced labour, he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> after rebelling and returned to lead the northern tribes in rejecting Solomon's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rehoboam">Rehoboam</a>. He ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shechem">Shechem</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirzah">Tirzah</a> and set up royal sanctuaries with golden calves at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bethel">Bethel</a> and Dan to rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jeroboam-i.jpg" alt="Jeroboam I" width="320" height="364" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Honoré Fragonard · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jean-Honor%C3%A9_Fragonard_-_Jeroboam_Offering_Sacrifice_for_the_Idol_-_WGA08049_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
